    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Fenelon Properties are delighted to bring to the market Dun Ard, Friars Hill, an impressive four-bedroom detached split-level residence occupying a generous and mature site in a highly convenient location close to Wicklow Town.\r\nSet well back from the road behind a substantial entrance and generous driveway, Dun Ard is a distinctive family home offering spacious and highly versatile accommodation arranged across multiple levels. The property has been well maintained and upgraded over the years and combines generous living accommodation with a particularly impressive rear garden, excellent parking and a range of useful outbuildings.\r\nThe principal living accommodation is positioned on the upper level and comprises a welcoming entrance hall, separate living room and an impressive open-plan kitchen, dining and family area. The kitchen is fitted with an extensive range of contemporary units with timber worktops and integrated appliances, while the adjoining living/dining area provides an excellent everyday family space. A bright sunroom overlooks and provides direct access to the rear garden. A guest WC completes this level.\r\nThe sleeping accommodation is located on the lower split level and comprises four bedrooms (one ensuite) together with the main bathroom, creating a good separation between the living and bedroom areas.\r\nAt lower-ground/basement level, the former garage has been converted to provide a substantial multi-purpose room with an adjoining en-suite. This is a particularly useful addition to the property and lends itself to a variety of uses such as a home office, games room, gym, hobby room or additional family space. \r\nExternally, Dun Ard sits on a particularly generous plot. A large driveway to the front provides excellent off-street parking, while pedestrian access leads around the property to the rear.\r\nThe long rear garden is a major feature of the property, predominantly laid in lawn and bordered by mature hedging, trees and established planting. A patio area immediately adjoining the house provides an attractive space for outdoor dining and entertaining, while the depth of the garden makes it particularly well suited to family use. There are also various outbuildings and storage areas, providing valuable additional space.\r\nThe property benefits from oil-fired central heating and mains services.\r\nFriars Hill is a sought-after and established residential location, combining a mature setting with excellent accessibility to Wicklow Town and its wide range of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, sporting facilities and everyday amenities. The property is also conveniently positioned for access to the N11/M11, making it an attractive option for commuters.\r\n\r\nDun Ard represents a superb opportunity to acquire a substantial and versatile detached family home on a generous site in one of Wicklow Town's established residential locations.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by appointment with Fenelon Properties."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall – 2.70m x 2.10m + 0.81m x 6.02m\r\nBright and welcoming entrance hall providing access to the principal living accommodation and split-level staircase to the bedroom accommodation below. Panelled walls and vaulted ceiling.\r\nLiving Room – Measurement TBC\r\nGenerous and bright separate reception room featuring a large picture window, timber-effect flooring and an attractive feature fireplace with stone surround. Double doors connect with the adjoining family/living accommodation.\r\nOpen-Plan Kitchen / Dining / Family Area – 3.22m x 6.70m + 5.47m x 2.99m\r\nImpressive and spacious family living area extending across the rear of the property. The contemporary fitted kitchen incorporates an extensive range of white shaker-style eye and floor-level units, timber worktops, tiled splashback and integrated appliances. Large window overlooking the garden, recessed lighting and timber-effect flooring. Generous dining and family areas provide excellent space for everyday living and entertaining.\r\nSunroom – 3.35m x 3.34m\r\nBright sunroom overlooking the mature rear garden with extensive glazing and direct access to the adjoining patio and garden. Tiled floor.\r\nGuest WC – 1.71m x 1.80m\r\nWC and wash-hand basin.\r\nLower Split Level\r\nBedroom 1 – Front – 2.97m x 4.10m\r\nGenerous double bedroom.\r\nBedroom 2 – Front – 3.01m x 3.02m\r\nWell-proportioned double bedroom with carpet flooring.\r\nBedroom 3 – 2.96m x 2.91m\r\nDouble bedroom.\r\nEnsuite:\r\nWc, whb and corner shower.\r\nBedroom 4 – 2.91m x 3.63m\r\nDouble bedroom with laminate timber-effect flooring and sliding fitted wardrobe.\r\nBathroom – 1.93m x 2.70m\r\nComprising WC, wash-hand basin and glazed corner shower enclosure with Triton electric shower. Fitted storage and shelving, timber-effect flooring and window providing natural light.\r\nLower Ground / Basement Level\r\nMulti-Purpose Room 1 – 5.33m x 3.20m\r\nGenerous additional room with laminate timber-effect flooring, sink and fitted shelving. Suitable for a variety of uses including home office, games room, gym or additional living space.\r\nMulti-Purpose Room 2 – 2.78m x 3.89m\r\nUseful adjoining room with laminate timber-effect flooring, offering further flexible ancillary accommodation.\r\nBathroom – 1.48m x 2.94m\r\nBathroom serving the lower-ground accommodation comprising WC, wash-hand basin and shower.\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nDun Ard occupies a generous mature site with a substantial driveway to the front providing excellent off-street parking for several vehicles.\r\nThe long rear garden is a particularly attractive feature, predominantly laid in lawn and bordered by mature hedging, trees and established planting. A paved patio area immediately adjoining the house provides an ideal outdoor seating and entertaining space.\r\nA number of outbuildings and storage areas provide useful ancillary space."
      },
